FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the FerrionOS patches before it in recipe.toml applied, ferrion-gpu-blob-submit.patch last among them. Submissions and the blob and context commands share virtio-gpud's control queue in request order:
- virtio-core: Queue::send_now places a chain on the ring now or gives it back, registering the waker to be woken when descriptors come free.
- virtio-gpud/src/submit.rs: submissions that find the ring full wait in order in the driver and are placed before any later submission; every command that waits for the device first places them, blocking until the ring has room. Completions are harvested by virtio-core's interrupt thread, so that wait never depends on the driver's own event loop.

